      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 97,
      "outputTokens": 749,
      "costUsd": 0.0067894999999999995,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a graph made the same way, for four different repayments. Each curve ends where its balance reaches zero, so you can read each term off the time axis. Thirty years, about twenty-two, about sixteen, and about thirteen. Each step up is another five hundred dollars a month. But the first five hundred saves almost six years, and the next saves only about three. On these curves, each extra five hundred dollars buys less time than the one before."
    },
