      "inputTokens": 112,
      "outputTokens": 744,
      "costUsd": 0.006751999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "This matters most for someone paying the thirty-year repayment. With a rate fixed at six per cent from the start, paying two thousand one hundred and forty-seven dollars twenty-nine stretches the term to almost forty-five years. At six and a half per cent, the first month's interest is two thousand one hundred and sixty-six dollars sixty-seven. That's more than the repayment, so the balance grows, and the loan is never repaid. A loan only shrinks when the repayment is more than the interest on the balance."
    },
