      "outputTokens": 567,
      "costUsd": 0.005144,
      "pronunciationText": "The monthly rate is half a per cent, so the first month's interest is half a per cent of two hundred thousand, which is one thousand dollars. That's the whole repayment. None of it reduces the debt, so the balance is still two hundred thousand next month, and the same thing happens every month. Two hundred months is wrong. Dividing the loan by the repayment ignores the interest."
